ALL BEUKERS-REDUCTION SYSTEM CHECKS PASSED

READING.  Beukers' refined Siegel-Shidlovskii theorem applies to (1,E0,E1,M_0..M_{d-2})
at every algebraic xi != 0.  Hence:

   [ int_0^1 e^{xi g(u)} du is transcendental for all nonconstant g in Qbar[u],
     all algebraic xi != 0 ]
                                    <==>
   [ (R):  M_0 is not in span_{Qbar(z)} {1, E_0, E_1, M_1, ..., M_{d-2}} ]

(R) is the concrete, finite form of opus-S4's "horizontal-endomorphism rigidity".
At d = 2 the span is {1, E_0, E_1} and (R) is exactly opus-S4's distinct-rate lemma
-- which is why degree 2 is closed.  For d >= 3 the M_1..M_{d-2} enter and (R) is
open.  The natural tool for it is the max-modulus Laplace asymptotic of
THM-3018 sec 4b, which already holds at every degree and for complex coefficients.

